   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let \\( g \\) be the function defined by \\( g(x) = \\int_{2}^{x} \\left(-(t - 1)(t - 6)(t - 9)\\right) \\, dt \\) for \\( 0 < x < 8 \\). Find the value of \\( x \\) at which \\( g \\) has a relative maximum."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 1
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "By the Fundamental Theorem of Calculus, \\( g'(x) = -(x - 1)(x - 6)(x - 9) \\) for \\( 0 < x < 8 \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Add",
               1,
               [
                  "Negate",
                  "x"
               ]
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               -9
            ],
            [
               "Add",
               "x",
               -6
            ]
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Set \\( g'(x) = 0 \\) and factor: \\( -(x - 1)(x - 6)(x - 9) = 0 \\), so \\( x = 1, 6, 9 \\).",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Only \\( x = 1 \\) and \\( x = 6 \\) lie in \\( 0 < x < 8 \\); \\( x = 9 \\) is outside the interval on which \\( g \\) is defined, so it is not a critical point of \\( g \\).",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "\\( g' \\) changes from positive to negative at \\( x = 1 \\) and from negative to positive at \\( x = 6 \\), so \\( g \\) has its relative maximum at \\( x = 1 \\).",
         "mathjson": 1
      }
   ],
